  "overview": "**Protocol** is a light-first design system anchored on `#ffffff` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#cb9eff` brand accent.\n\nDisplay headlines pair `Mozilla Headline` with `Inter` body copy (56px display down to 16px body), unified by `4px` base corner radius and subtle shadow elevation.\n\nMaintained by **Mozilla**. Source: published token package (https://github.com/mozilla/protocol), repo https://github.com/mozilla/protocol, package `@mozilla-protocol/core`, frameworks: css. Inventory: **91** colors, **32** typography steps, and **16** documented components (MPL-2.0 license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 16 component tokens with documented paddings: `8px 16px`, `32px 4px`, `0 32px 0 6px`, `10px 18px`, `9px 13px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#f9f9fb` cards; separate sibling sections using `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Layered Shadow Model**: Uses documented shadows (`0 16px 16px -16px rgba(0,0,0,.3)`) paired with `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` borders for elevated overlays.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#cb9eff` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#ffffff` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#cb9eff` with `#0b0b0c` text (9.3:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `Mozilla Headline` headings with `Inter` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `4px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (4px on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `#f9f9fb` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `4px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input-default` fields and secondary buttons."
